# Retail fast-file record layouts (docs/design/FASTFILE_LOADER.md, "Design").
# A retail .ff stores every record in its 32-bit (ILP32) layout. Each record is
# described once, in its family's file under disk32/, which this file
# includes; scripts/gen_disk32.py turns them into the disk32 mirror structs and
# the 64-bit loaders at build time. Generated code is never committed
# (AGENTS.md rule 8).
#
# The included files are read in name order, and the generated headers follow
# that order. A family's file is <NN>-<family>.schema: NN is the order the
# family converted in, so a new family takes the next number. Families that
# share a number sort by name, and order has no other meaning.
#
#   record <Name> <retail size> runtime=<native struct> header=<its header> [same=<disk32:: constant>]
#          [copy=scalars]
#       [asset member=<XAssetHeader member> pool=<publish call> kind=<DBAliasKind>
#              alias=<inserted|completed> label=<noun> [name=<field>] [body=custom] [check=custom]]
#       <retail offset> <field> <kind>[<n>]... [count=<expression>] [of=<record>] [terminated] [paired]
#               [label=<noun>]
#
# Kinds: i32 u32 f32 i16 u16 u8 (scalars), bool (one byte; nonzero is true),
# xstring (a C string: inline or an offset token), bytes (inline bytes, count
# given), xstrings (a pointer array of C strings, count given), pointer (a
# token only a custom body loads), rawptr (pointer bytes that are no token;
# the loader nulls them), array (count elements of=<an earlier record without
# an asset line>, label=<noun>), struct (that record inline, of=<record>; only
# a custom body loads it). A scalar other than bool may be a fixed array, as
# knots f32[8][2]; a generated body copies it whole. So may a pointer, for a
# custom body, as an impact entry's effects pointer[29]. A dotted field
# (sound.info.rate) is a member of a nested native struct: its mirror member
# takes the last name, and only a custom body or copy=scalars loads it.
# copy=scalars emits Copy<Name>Scalars for a custom body: every scalar and
# fixed array, and null for every rawptr.
# The offsets and sizes are the retail facts: the generator checks them
# against the ILP32 rules, and the compiler checks the emitted mirror against
# them (ONDISK_*) and the native struct against the same field list (RUNTIME_*).
#
# An asset line makes the record a top-level asset family with a generated
# 64-bit loader: the header-slot entry, the pointer step and, unless
# body=custom, the record body. The family's TU defines DB_Load<Name>PtrDisk32
# by forwarding to db::disk32_load::Load<Name>HeaderSlot.
#   alias=inserted   as the 32-bit Load_<Name>Ptr with DB_InsertPointer: the
#                    pointer step pushes the temp block and the record streams
#                    there, the native header is a temporary the pool call
#                    copies, -2 registers the pooled pointer and an offset
#                    token resolves to it. The body is generated or custom.
#   alias=completed  as with DB_RegisterPointerSlot and DB_CompleteObject: the
#                    record streams at the current position, the hand-written
#                    body converts it into zone-lifetime native storage, and an
#                    offset token resolves to that native object. The body
#                    is custom.
#   name=<field>     the xstring the pool hashes; the generated body drops a
#                    null one.
#   check=custom     the 32-bit loader's further rules on the converted record:
#                    a hand-written Check<Name> in the family's TU, called
#                    after every field loads; false drops.
#   label=<noun>     names the family, or a bytes field, in error messages.
# A generated body streams the record into its mirror and copies the scalars
# (bool as != 0). It then pushes block 4 and loads each xstring, bytes and
# array field in schema order. An array streams its retail elements, then
# converts each into zone-lifetime native storage, loading its strings. A
# bytes field there must be terminated: count is <field> or <field>+<n>,
# checked, and the last byte must be 0. A paired one is present exactly when
# its count field is nonzero.

include disk32/*.schema
